# Runs the Node-only half of CrossByte against Node.
#
# ci/js-tests.hxml is the portable suite: no socket, no subprocess, no runtime
# driving itself, because every case in it has to mean the same thing on the
# browser build. That leaves everything written for Node specifically -- the
# self-driven loop, sockets over js.node.net, URLLoader over Node's HTTP
# client, NativeProcess over child_process -- with no suite to sit in.
#
# It is a program rather than a set of fixtures because what it covers is
# asynchronous, and because one of those things owns the process: a loop that
# drives itself cannot be tested from inside a harness already driving a
# runtime of its own.
-cp src
-cp tests
-lib hxnodejs
-main NodeIntegrationMain
--js export/js-runtime-tests/runtime.js
--macro crossbyte.test.SuiteCoverage.check()
